{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_017unMm2k1b9pzaXncZ2Jdj1", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.Wikipedia.com/wiki/Harees\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildlife_of_Zanzibar\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es/BVMDefensa/cartocuba/en/consulta_aut/registro.do?id=432192\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es/BVMDefensa/pacifico/en/consulta_aut/registro.do?id=432192\"}, {\"url\": \"https://superstock.com/asset/zanzibar-from-arabic-zanjibar-from-persian-zangibar-coast-blacks-zangi/1899-18852273\"}, {\"url\": \"https://graphsearch.epfl.ch/en/concept/34414\"}, {\"url\": \"https://album-online.com/detail/de/ZjdjNDA5MA/zanzibar-from-arabic-zanjibar-persian-zangibar-coast-blacks-zangi-black-alb5536626\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Kidichi\"}, {\"url\": \"https://travelfeed.io/@ammrito/zanzibar-island-tanzania\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:33:48.533Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Harees Zanzibar called", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01YcVX9G9cDtwiHJq4MB21Lp", "content": [{"title": "en.wikipedia.com", "url": "https://en.Wikipedia.com/wiki/Harees"}, {"title": "Wildlife of Zanzibar", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildlife_of_Zanzibar"}, {"title": "bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es", "url": "https://bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es/BVMDefensa/cartocuba/en/consulta_aut/registro.do?id=432192"}, {"title": "bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es", "url": "https://bibliotecavirtual.defensa.gob.es/BVMDefensa/pacifico/en/consulta_aut/registro.do?id=432192"}, {"title": "superstock.com", "url": "https://superstock.com/asset/zanzibar-from-arabic-zanjibar-from-persian-zangibar-coast-blacks-zangi/1899-18852273"}, {"title": "graphsearch.epfl.ch", "url": "https://graphsearch.epfl.ch/en/concept/34414"}, {"title": "zanzibar from arabic zanjibar persian zangibar coast blacks zangi black alb5536626", "url": "https://album-online.com/detail/de/ZjdjNDA5MA/zanzibar-from-arabic-zanjibar-persian-zangibar-coast-blacks-zangi-black-alb5536626"}, {"title": "en.wikipedia.com", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.com/wiki/Kidichi"}, {"title": "Zanzibar Island, Tanzania", "url": "https://travelfeed.io/@ammrito/zanzibar-island-tanzania"}]}, "The search found one direct answer. A Wikipedia entry on harees lists a Zanzibari version under the name boko boko, which it says may be made with lamb, beef, or chicken. The same page describes harees more broadly as a dish made from wheat and meat, and says it is a popular dish mainly in the Harari region of Ethiopia.\n\nThe other results are about Zanzibar itself, not the dish. The name Zanzibar comes from Persian and Arabic words meaning roughly \"coast of the blacks,\" and the islands are known for spices. None of them mention harees or boko boko. I found only one source for the Zanzibari name, and it was a Wikipedia mirror, so it's worth checking against a Swahili or Zanzibari cooking source before relying on it."], "durationSeconds": 4.868153, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_017unMm2k1b9pzaXncZ2Jdj1", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
