{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01DMsFsNkEiSqBZWMXssxjV4", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://encycloreader.org/r/wikipedia.php?q=Harees\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.Wikipedia.com/wiki/Harees\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wiki.krisyotam.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic_2026-03/Harees\"}, {\"url\": \"https://clovegarden.com/recipes/qmm_cowwht1.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://standardmedia.co.ke/amp/-1'%20OR%203*2%3C(0%205%20597-597)%20--%20/article/2001500896/kenya-ismaili-imamat-sign-mou-on-climate-health-and-education\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hellskitchen.206.189.43.227.sslip.io/dish/3625\"}, {\"url\": \"https://standardmedia.co.ke/evewoman/food/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.standardmedia.co.ke/evewoman/living/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hellskitchen.206.189.43.227.sslip.io/dish/1362\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:33:56.794Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "boko boko Zanzibar harees wheat meat dish", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01SxMbEzzQ4CzFt42Zc2e4wj", "content": [{"title": "encycloreader.org", "url": "https://encycloreader.org/r/wikipedia.php?q=Harees"}, {"title": "en.wikipedia.com", "url": "https://en.Wikipedia.com/wiki/Harees"}, {"title": "wiki.krisyotam.com", "url": "https://wiki.krisyotam.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic_2026-03/Harees"}, {"title": "Dish of Beef & Wheat Bokoboko", "url": "https://clovegarden.com/recipes/qmm_cowwht1.html"}, {"title": "Swahili Boko Boko delight (Photo: iStock)", "url": "https://standardmedia.co.ke/amp/-1'%20OR%203*2%3C(0%205%20597-597)%20--%20/article/2001500896/kenya-ismaili-imamat-sign-mou-on-climate-health-and-education"}, {"title": "Boko Boko Harees", "url": "https://hellskitchen.206.189.43.227.sslip.io/dish/3625"}, {"title": "easy recipe swahili boko boko delight", "url": "https://standardmedia.co.ke/evewoman/food/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight"}, {"title": "easy recipe swahili boko boko delight", "url": "https://www.standardmedia.co.ke/evewoman/living/article/2001500896/easy-recipe-swahili-boko-boko-delight"}, {"title": "hellskitchen.206.189.43.227.sslip.io", "url": "https://hellskitchen.206.189.43.227.sslip.io/dish/1362"}]}, "Boko boko is the Zanzibari name for harees, a wheat-and-meat porridge found across the Middle East, Horn of Africa, and East Africa.\n\n- **Zanzibar and East Africa:** Wikipedia mirrors say in Zanzibar, the dish is called boko boko and may be cooked with lamb, beef, or chicken. One mirror adds that this same dish is also served across Tanzania and Kenya.\n- **Origins:** A Kenyan recipe article says it was brought down to the coast of East Africa by Middle Eastern settlers.\n- **Recipe:** The Kenyan recipe uses cracked wheat, rice, whole spices such as cinnamon, cardamom and black pepper, cubed steak, and ghee. The cook is pressure-cooked, then the mixture is pounded until it mashes. The Kenyan article notes that people often have it with some ghee and sugar. A Tanzanian-style beef version from a recipe site is cooked with onion, garlic, ginger, cumin and pepper, and can be cooked dry, almost like steamed rice, but it can also be quite liquid, like a stew.\n- **Occasions:** Across the Gulf, harees is an iftar staple in Ramadan, and in Ethiopia's Harari region it is served on Eid or special occasions such as the birth of a baby.\n\nSource caveats: the Wikipedia content comes through several mirrors, and one of them carries a \"citation needed\" tag on the Ethiopian claim. The Burundian boko boko page is a recipe site with no clear sourcing, so I'd treat its details as unverified."], "durationSeconds": 5.678772874999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01DMsFsNkEiSqBZWMXssxjV4", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
